          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2500583">Count Smiley</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP576 Eaton Road&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Had to locate the trowel buried in the car before we could uncover the face of this one.  Well, at least this trip we remembered to bring the trowel!  TFTCap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="632391168">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-08-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="228846">Mr. CanoeHead</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP576 Eaton Road

It's amazing how a well concealed and buried cap like this one can be so beaten up yet the exposed ones out in William Switzer were pristine.  Used the metal detector and the trowel to find and expose this one.    We took a context shot and the shot of the cap to confirm our visit.   TFTCap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="509964154">
